{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneChiralityInvolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneChiralityInvolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneChiralityInvolution.conjugate_two_content_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneChiralityInvolution.conjugate_two_content_flip","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneChiralityInvolution.lean#L58-L61","doc":"A concrete transpose pair `[2] ↔ [1,1]` exhibits the chirality flip\n`c(λ') = − c(λ)` that C2 forces (here `c([2]) = 1`, `c([1,1]) = −1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneChiralityInvolution.electron_content_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneChiralityInvolution.electron_content_zero","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneChiralityInvolution.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The self-conjugate electron block is **chirality-neutral**: content sum `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneChiralityInvolution.electron_self_conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneChiralityInvolution.electron_self_conjugate","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneChiralityInvolution.lean#L50-L53","doc":"The electron block `(3,1,1)` is **self-conjugate** (a transpose fixed point).\nPer the keystone, `(3,1,1) = T₁ ⊕ T₂` is the self-conjugate A₅ rep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneChiralityInvolution.cellContent_transpose_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneChiralityInvolution.cellContent_transpose_neg","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneChiralityInvolution.lean#L43-L48","doc":"**Chirality atom.**  A cell's content `c(i,j) = j − i` negates under transpose\n`(i,j) ↦ (j,i)`.  Since chirality is the sign of the content, transpose flips\nchirality — the involution C2 forces. ","signatureChunk":0}]}